-- title:
--   Cyclotomic determinant forces detρ̄(c)=-1
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $p$ be a prime, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) = \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ which is trivial on the elements fixing some finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ pointwise. Assume that $\bar\rho$, regarded as an adic Galois representation over the local ring $k$ via [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196), has cyclotomic determinant in the sense of `DetIsCyclotomic` for $p$: the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $k$ (so $p = 0$ in $k$), and for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$, all $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and all $a \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\sigma(\mu) = \mu^{a}$ for every $\mu \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mu^{p^{n}} = 1$, the element $\det \bar\rho(\sigma) - a$ lies in the ideal of $k$ generated by $p^{n}$. Then the determinant of the endomorphism $\bar\rho(c)$ equals $-1$, where $c$ is [`complexConjugation`](def/GaloisRep_ComplexConjugation.html#L30), the restriction to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of complex conjugation of $\mathbb{C}$ as a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism.
--
--   This is the standard oddness statement: a two-dimensional residual representation whose determinant is the mod $p$ cyclotomic character satisfies $\det\bar\rho(c) = -1$. It supplies the archimedean input for the Euler-characteristic computation bounding Selmer groups, and is cited in the bound for the rank of the strict Selmer group in terms of the number of Taylor–Wiles primes and the rank of the dual Selmer group.
